<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14350" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dispunctĭo</span></b> ,
		ōnis, f.
		dispungo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a settling up, balancing</i> of accounts (late
			Lat.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">concedenda creditoribus (with recognitio),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					42, 5, 15</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>an investigation,
				examination, a testing</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">boni et mali operis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Marc. 5, 12</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">utriusque meriti,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Apol. 18</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vitae,</span>”
				i. e. <i>death</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. Test. Anim. 4</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. de Anim. 33 <i>fin.</i></span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
